By the sublimation method, 2H-type SiC whiskers were obtained. From the experi
mental results and the results from the heating experiments of powdered mixture of high
pure silicon and graphite, the thermal stability of the basic polytypes of SiC were discussed. The conclusions are summarized as follows;
1) The ƒÀ-SiC grow in the whole range of temperature under the condition of high supersaturation.
2) Initial phase appeared from ƒÀ-SiC with heatings is mainly 6H above 1600•Ž and mainly 4H or 2H below 1400•Ž.
3) Each basic polytypes of SiC, 2H, 3C, 4H, and 6H is stable in the range of tem
perature, below 1400•Ž, 1400•`1600•Ž, 1600•`2100•Ž, and above 2100•Ž respectively. The 15 R-type is unstable form in the whole range of temperature. [Received Sept. 16, 1969]
